Context: T052 (looper:finding:macos-normalizepath-symlink). The macOS check job failed because the test pinned normalizePath output against a literal t.TempDir string, while macOS resolves the temp dir's /var ancestor to /private/var. Decision: fix the test, not normalizePath — parent-symlink resolution is the documented one-key-per-file invariant (NOTES.md, T005), so the expectation must go through filepath.EvalSymlinks; special-casing darwin in the function would split /tmp and /private/tmp keys. Linux behavior is unchanged (expectation is byte-identical when TMPDIR is not a symlink). macOS condition reproduced on Linux by running the test with TMPDIR behind a symlink (fails before, passes after); full make check and make build pass. Gotcha for reproduction: keep the symlinked TMPDIR short — a long one trips the 108-byte unix-socket path limit in the serve e2e tests. Actual macOS execution remains unverified from this Linux worker; the next macOS CI run on the integrated commit confirms it.
